# MERGE-PARENT-MODEL-SOURCE (steps/defects.md): the model and the candidate are different places.  u1 copies User
# with C, a copy of the unit holding a1', a1's instance as the merge saw it (x 1); the root then writes a1\x: 5 into
# the original only.  Run, u1's code reads x of its candidate, the root's a1 (the caller's binding first), through
# its own copied requirement a1' -- 5 -- while a1' keeps 1.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Model:
    int: x 1
end: Model
a1: merge: Model
User:
    int: y 0
    y: a1\x
end: User
u1: merge: User
a1\x: 5
u1
int: ok 7
if: u1\y != 5
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
